\fs28 \cf2 \cb13 You can use any editor or IDE that you like. If you're using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://code.visualstudio.com/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Visual Studio Code}} you can take advantage of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=modular-mojotools.vscode-mojo"}}{\fldrslt \ul Mojo for Visual Studio Code extension}}, which provides features like syntax highlighting, code completion, and debugging support. For {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cursor.com/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Cursor}} and other editors that support VS Code extensions, you can install the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open-vsx.org/extension/modular-mojotools/vscode-mojo"}}{\fldrslt \ul Mojo for Visual Studio Code extension}} from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open-vsx.org/"}}{\fldrslt \ul Open VSX Registry}}. See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.modular.com/stable/mojo/manual/install/#add-the-vs-code-extension"}}{\fldrslt \ul Add the VS Code extension}} for more information.\cb1 \
