\cf2 An executable Mojo program requires you to define a no-argument 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 main()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function as its entry point. Running the program automatically invokes the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 main()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function, and your program exits when the 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb12 main()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  function returns.\
To run the program, we first need to start a shell session in our project's virtual environment:\
